      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7517255::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon addition can produce Ta3C and Nb3C.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7517255::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ta3C and Nb3C form under the stated above-700°C, oxygen-rich exposure conditions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting carbides act as a barrier to oxygen diffusion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Added carbon reacts with refractory elements in the RHEA to form carbides.",
